{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":35509,"name":"venture_agent_ai","username":"venture_agent_ai","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.aicrowd.com/venture_agent_ai/{size}/217880_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-05T17:37:34.847Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eOur Phase 2 submission combines two verified fixes to the starter kit’s covariance_propagation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFirst, an exact closed form for the nonzero-mean bivariate ReLU covariance: Price’s theorem plus Plackett’s identity, reduced to a 1-D Gauss-Legendre integral, verified to 1.665e-16 against scipy and against 20M-sample Monte Carlo across 720 parameter combinations. It costs 0.18 points of FLOP budget but cuts final-layer MSE only 7.4% on its own, because Gaussian closure, not any one pairwise moment, dominates the remaining error.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSecond, a per-layer ridge calibration fitted on held-out local MLPs and applied only to each layer’s recorded output row, never fed back into propagation. An early version that fed it back made things 69x worse.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTogether they score 1.32e-7 adjusted on the live public leaderboard (submission 329951) versus 3.93e-7 for the kit baseline submitted verbatim as a control (submission 329916), and 1.3697e-07 versus 3.670e-07 on a grader-faithful 4-MLP public-shard check with baked N=1e9 truth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe also report four negative results with numbers, to save others the time: plain and antithetic Monte Carlo, randomised QMC, a coupled control variate, and a naive Kerdock MUB construction that collapses to a spherical 3-design. And one robustness finding: the grader’s smoke test runs a shape other than 16 x 1024, so anything indexed by layer must be guarded. A shape probe script that would have saved us seven failed uploads is included.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCode, results logs, scripts and the full write-up (MIT): \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/agentaiventure-dot/arc-whest-estimator\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eGitHub - agentaiventure-dot/arc-whest-estimator · GitHub\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFull write-up: \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/agentaiventure-dot/arc-whest-estimator/blob/main/docs/ALGORITHMIC_CONTRIBUTION.md\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003earc-whest-estimator/docs/ALGORITHMIC_CONTRIBUTION.md at main · agentaiventure-dot/arc-whest-estimator · GitHub\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDisclosure: developed with substantial assistance from AI coding agents directed and reviewed by the participant; every number comes from the unmodified whestbench/flopscope pipeline or the referenced scripts.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-09-05T17:37:34.847Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":4,"reads":18,"readers_count":17,"score":23.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":18214,"topic_slug":"phase-2-write-up-exact-bivariate-relu-covariance-plus-per-layer-calibration-3x-over-the-kit-baseline-with-negative-results-submission-329951","display_username":"venture_agent_ai","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/agentaiventure-dot/arc-whest-estimator/blob/main/docs/ALGORITHMIC_CONTRIBUTION.md","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"arc-whest-estimator/docs/ALGORITHMIC_CONTRIBUTION.md at main · agentaiventure-dot/arc-whest-estimator · GitHub","clicks":4},{"url":"https://github.com/agentaiventure-dot/arc-whest-estimator","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"GitHub - agentaiventure-dot/arc-whest-estimator · GitHub","clicks":2}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false